{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"quasiempty-snug-phoenix","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\ncuddly-callous-antlion (fixed in 844dd26b854) showed CI unit workers stall for seconds: the py3.11 job spent 4.78 s in a test whose work takes 0.3 s, and the same run took 1.751 s in a fixture that only sets environment variables. Three other \"hang-guard\" tests assert a wall-clock ceiling whose margin is smaller than or close to stalls of that size:\n- `tests/unit/test_doctor_mapping.py:315`: `elapsed < 4.0` against a probe that sleeps 5.0 s; a 4 s stall fails it, and the margin over the 5 s failure mode is 1 s.\n- `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py:2311`: `elapsed < 2.0` for a lifespan shutdown; a 2 s stall fails it.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py:168`: `elapsed < 5.0` for a refusal that takes microseconds; a 5 s stall fails it.\n\n## Expected\nEach test proves its property (the hang was abandoned, the shutdown was bounded, the refusal did not queue) by an ordering or state observation that a descheduled test process cannot break, as 844dd26b854 did for test_llm_timeouts.py.\n\n## Plan\n1. Reproduce: run each test under a scratch pytest plugin that pauses the process for longer than its ceiling partway through (the method used for cuddly-callous-antlion), recording the failure.\n2. Replace each wall-clock ceiling with an observation of what happened (for example, the abandoned probe's thread is still sleeping when scan_mapping returns; the lifespan's own bound fired rather than the outer safety net; admission raised without acquiring), keeping each test's ability to catch the real defect: re-introduce the defect (unbounded probe wait, unbounded lifespan cancel, blocking acquire) and show the test fails.\n3. Run the 3 test files, make lint (including the wall-clock-assert gate), make typecheck.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Each of the 3 tests passes 3 of 3 runs under a pause longer than its former ceiling.\n- [ ] Re-introducing each test's defect makes that test fail.\n- [ ] make lint and make typecheck exit 0, and the change merges with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- tests/unit/test_doctor_mapping.py\n- tests/unit/test_review_bot.py\n- tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py","id":"8171-28d0-68b7-4ba6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"3 hang-guard tests assert wall-clock ceilings that CI worker stalls exceed"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793487452284956001,"uuid":"fa5f54bc-7766-4689-95f1-8cf4b1c531d1"}